ped with `OnPolicyFetchCompleted`, although it's a bit more difficult"],["1345e5b5_40385507",63,-11,1,"might wanna log in this branch"],["198f765a_d6da3d0b",70,-11,0,"ugh, I really wish `BarrierCallback` could automatically handle this case for us. But it doesn't"],["27a2ea87_e36e705f",71,-11,0,"Should be `barrier_callback`. Same in the other branch"],["3234c171_17da925d",63,-11,0,"This doesn't work in the multiple-extensions-in-one-request case, correct?"],["39d5b777_6ffd6b2f",72,-11,1,"nit: forward-declare `struct ExtensionIdAndVersion` instead"],["45f6368b_9c6845c2",63,-11,1,"90% of this method is copied from `FetchPolicy(reason)`. Can you dedupe this? e.g. `FetchPolicy(reason)` internally calls `FetchPolicy(reason, nullopt, OnceCallback<void(Value)>())` and then the…"],["4a4a23ab_eb5ff13f",63,-11,1,"This is abusing the existing API: the current FetchPolicy method fetches `types_to_fetch_` when you call it.... but now this new API can fetch things that *aren't* in `types_to_fetch_`. That's very…"],["5cabd2fe_edc1ee74",63,-11,0,"tangential nit: I see this: ``` CloudPolicyClientTypeParams( const string& policy_type, RepeatingCallback<set<ExtensionIdAndVersion>()> extension_ids_and_version_getter); ``` wouldn't it be easier…"],["6e84cb73_c49bb1ce",73,-11,0,"same as CloudPolicyClient::FetchPolicy(), any chance we can dedupe this or make one impl call the other?"],["92f39aaa_a0bc71b6",63,-11,1,"You should still call `callback` if the operation fails. Same for every other branch in this function, too: whoever calls `FetchPolicy` would expect `callback` to get called. Otherwise there could be…"],["99efc10d_d5e2c20e",63,-11,1,"What if it doesn't parse? Check the retval and log something"],["b1c386e3_915e92b8",71,-11,0,"nit: this is bitwise-and not logical-and. It _works_ in this case since `true` is normally 1, but better to be explicit about the intent IMO: ``` bool success = std::ranges::all_of(results,…"],["c17e0bb9_77ea7312",72,-11,1,"nit: remove this method. it's unimplemented and not needed anymore"],["c288bb2c_36a2ab5b",73,-11,1,"I don't understand this change. Why the extra braces here?"],["c3e01b1d_b5fcdaec",72,-11,1,"nit: #include <optional>"],["fb9fb96e_96da58f2",71,-11,1,"optional suggestion, but maybe this is too \"clever\": ``` std::array services = {service(), extension_install_service()}; int count = std::ranges::count_if(services, std::identity{}); if (count == 0)…"],["426fd8ec_80deb270",63,-10,1,"So `CloudPolicyClientTypeParams` right now is basically: ``` struct CloudPolicyClientTypeParams { string policy_type; string settings_entity_id; // (possibly empty-string) set<string>…"],["50abe0a8_d6c9495a",70,-10,1,"This should be `extension_id@extension_version`, right? Same above"],["67dfa6e2_95e5fd94",63,-10,0,"I notice that callers are sending some redundant information. ``` machine_cloud_policy_manager->core() ->extension_install_service() ->FetchPolicy( CloudPolicyClientTypeParams(…"],["6db02d46_421035fa",63,-10,1,"Actually since the two methods fetch different \"things\" and have very different semantics, maybe 2 public methods is fine? But still share the implementation: ``` public:…"],["7a6752e8_6fb26307",70,-10,1,"Add an appropriate `PolicyFetchReason` enum val"],["8bad27f5_a65bc6ae",63,-10,0,"Maybe for another CL: can you implement `operator<<` for `CloudPolicyClientTypeParams` instead? That way we can print `extension_ids_and_version()` too for debugging"],["e67c1d13_3ba5f527",63,-10,1,"if you implement my API suggestion below: revert to `CHECK(!types_to_fetch_.empty());`"],["03d23e6d_5d38ba47",71,-4,0,"Why is this the case? Does this mean if I call `extension_install_service()->RefreshPolicy()` it also refreshes normal policies? That would be strange..."],["0b882833_fbc5463e",74,-4,1,"still needed?"],["30667aab_d6f53da6",63,-4,1,"Instead of having this if/else, we could loop every time. That would dedupe some code. Make the caller pass a `const flat_set<TypeParams>&` instead of an `optional<TypeParams>`. `FetchPolicy()` would…"],["3631ab0b_fafcedcd",63,-4,1,"comment and code don't describe the same thing"],["4fe58497_a1240fab",63,-4,1,"Technically this isn't guaranteed to run if the server sends an incorrect payload, right? e.g. with 0 responses, or if we can't parse `ExtensionInstallPolicies`. We should still run the callback if…"],["5169c415_9d7fcb25",63,-4,1,"bad indent? or extra brace?"],["51faad74_acd731e6",75,-4,1,"nit: `const ExtensionIdAndVersion&`"],["617938ef_f4bd9dd8",71,-4,1,"`kExtensionInstall`?"],["635fb8c4_5f13f60b",62,-4,1,"nit: `const std::string&` or `std::string_view`"],["66e00809_c963b0a9",63,-4,1,"That's a *lot* of function parameters. Most of them are just private class fields: ``` public_key_version_valid_, public_key_version_, device_dm_token_, last_policy_timestamp_, invalidation_payload_,…"],["8e48362d_143500b5",70,-4,1,"nit: ``` bool can_install = std::all_of( values, [](auto action) { return action != em::ExtensionInstallPolicy::ACTION_BLOCK; }, &ExtensionInstallActionAndReasons::action); ```"],["a0a854be_e74d675d",63,-4,0,"NB this makes a copy"],["b757ec4c_0fce8a20",75,-4,1,"nit: `const std::string&` or `std::string_view`"],["db001c42_850344d8",64,-4,0,"optional very optional nit: kind of a long name; that tends to hurt readability. Maybe I'm overthinking it, but WDYT of putting it in a namespace? e.g. ``` namespace policy { namespace extensions {…"],["eff7c78f_97decc31",63,-4,1,"This param's type is a bit too specific. How about the caller passes a `DMServerJobConfiguration::Callback`, and *they* decide what the callback does with the `DMServerJobResult`. Basically…"],["f8e7e224_55b86155",64,-4,1,"other optional nit: I think the name \"Decision\" is shorter than \"ActionAndReasons\" and captures the same meaning. Or maybe \"InstallPolicy\" like the protobuf"],["04ef0fd4_40ead20e",76,-3,1,"nit: put `using ExtensionSetCallback = base::RepeatingCallback<...>` or whatever in this class, so we don't type out the templated type every time"],["15c5e30e_e04c684f",76,-3,0,"doesn't really matter but this could be `operator<=>` instead of `operator<` & `operator==`, since C++20"],["a7db4b7b_019f6ac5",76,-3,1,"This is not a `operator<` impl. i.e. you can have `a < b` and `b < a` both be false. Could lead to weird sorting in the `flat_set<>`. I never tried it, but apparently `std::variant<>` already…"],["b3f32ed3_030cf044",75,-3,1,"nit: add doc comment"],["c617427e_b84b6990",62,-3,1,"nit: add doc comments"],["f2fb1d19_b164e551",70,-3,1,"this is backwards, no?"],["feed2ded_f6f9a56c",63,-3,1,"nit: `s/enterprise_management::/em::/` across this file"],["7723e2ab_88a08fd7",63,0,0,"can you add a couple test cases in `cloud_policy_client_unittest.cc` or `cloud_policy_service_unittest.cc`?"]],0,773]]}